-- 6. Slide-attack preconditions -----------------------------
   a slide attack needs the round transform to repeat: identical
   subkeys AND identical round constants across rounds
   [PASS] all 16 round constants RC_i are distinct   16 distinct
   [PASS] no key produces two identical subkeys (50 000 keys)   0 keys
   Conclusion: the round function differs at every round even for a
   hypothetical key with repeated subkeys, so the classic slide
   attack has no self-similar structure to exploit.

